  body: "# IIDB injury, loss of faculty and disablement\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source distinguishes
    injury, impaired bodily or mental function, disability and the aggregate disablement assessment, rather than
    using all four terms interchangeably.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThese are IIDB assessment concepts, not
    universal disability definitions or a finding about any person. Conditions differ before and from 1 October
    1986, and accidents and prescribed diseases have exceptions. No percentage is assigned.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 69002, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 69003, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 69004, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 69005, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 69006, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 69007, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch69`:
    PDF `3bbd376d12fc0a6633010680e88d11efdf7f5b34dde311016a073e80ac3e56b8`; extracted pages `fcaf30907d52d71cc7473cf40c8c876469efc3f8d18f7f9af7b3d32bf5016d95`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.033473Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6172830bd3bf7f55f94795f8/dmgch69.pdf#page=2
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/iidb-assessment-boundaries
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter applies different assessment conditions by claim date, aggregation and disease.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0003
      quote: "69009 An employed earner was entitled to IIDB if, as a result of an IA, a loss of physical or mental
        faculty\n\noccurred for which the extent of disablement was assessed at not less than one 1% 1. A person
        with\npneumoconiosis was treated as having satisfied that condition irrespective of whether there was an\n\
        \nactual loss of faculty2.\n\n\n                                                                       \
        \          1 SS Act 75, s 57(1); 2 s 78(3)\n\n\n\nClaims made on or after 1.10.86"
      locator: DMG 69009
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0003
      quote: "69010 To become entitled to IIDB an employed earner must establish that\n\n\n1. as a result of an
        IA, a loss of physical or mental faculty occurs for which disablement is assessed at not\n\nless than 14%1or\n\
        \n\n2. as a result of more than one accident, losses of physical or mental faculty occur, for each of which\n\
        \ndisablement is assessed at less than 14% but which in total amount to 14% or more 2or\n\n\n3. in pneumoconiosis
        and byssinosis cases, disablement is assessed, or treated as assessed, at not less\n\nthan 1%3or\n\n\n4.
        in the case of claims for occupational deafness, disablement is assessed at not less than 20% 4.\n\n\n \
        \                           1 SS CB Act 92, s 103(1); 2 s 103(2)(a)(b); 3 SS (II) (PD) Regs, reg 20; 4 reg
        34(6)\n\n\n\nProvision of NINO"
      locator: DMG 69010
  - target: term/iidb-medical-nonmedical-questions
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Loss of faculty and disablement assessment are among the medical questions in the outcome
      decision.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0006
      quote: "69020 DMs will give an outcome decision on the claim which consists of a statement to the effect that\n\
        the claimant is either entitled or not entitled to benefit. In arriving at an outcome decision, the DM must\n\
        consider various questions. For IIDB, these questions fall into two categories\n\n\n1. non medical questions
        such as employed earners employment, rate of benefit 1and\n\n\n2. medical questions such as diagnosis, relevant
        loss of faculty and disablement assessment.\n\n\nNote: See DMG Chapter 01 for further guidance on IIDB decisions.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                       1 SS CB Act 92,
        s 94"
      locator: DMG 69020
